cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Chiquipoli: exact, interval and formal verification of the local maximality of A16, A32, A64, Z32 and Z64"
abstract: >-
  Exact-arithmetic, interval-arithmetic (256-bit) and Lean 4 certification that the
  Bingane-Audet equilateral small polygons A16, A32 and A64, and the larger-perimeter
  polygons Z32 and Z64 rebuilt from their description, are strict local maximisers of the
  perimeter among convex equilateral polygons of diameter at most one, modulo
  orientation-preserving Euclidean motions. The certificates check the hypotheses of a
  first-order criterion (strictly positive multipliers on the active diameters and
  K_eq = R(p)); the criterion itself, the five polygons and an explicit radius for A16
  (6.63e-4, by two Lean arguments) are formalised in Lean 4. Records of every run carry
  the Git commit, a clean-tree flag and SHA-256 hashes of the sources. The package
  accompanies the article "First-Order Geometry of Equilateral Small Polygons".
type: software
version: "1.3.1"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
